'''''Pulicaria microcephala''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] of the family [[Asteraceae]] [[endemic]] to the [[Berlengas|Berlengas archipelago]] in [[Portugal]]. It is a small and ramified plant<ref name="berlengas">{{cite web |title=Pulicária-das-Berlengas |url=https://www.berlengas.eu/pt/especie/pulicaria-das-berlengas/especie-alvo |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160207102625/http://berlengas.eu/pt/especie/pulicaria-das-berlengas/especie-alvo |url-status=usurped |archive-date=February 7, 2016 |publisher=berlengas.eu |accessdate=12 November 2020}}</ref> occurring in clearings of scrubs in coastal cliffs.<ref name=flora.on>{{cite web |title=Pulicaria microcephala |url=https://flora-on.pt/index.php#/7AQDE |publisher=Flora-on |accessdate=12 November 2020}}</ref> Its flowers are yellow, flowering between March and July.<ref name="berlengas" /><ref name= owleducaction>{{cite web |title=Pulicária-das-berlengas |url=https://www.owleducation.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/ANEXO-14.-Cartas-e-Chaves_Jogo-das-Berlengas03-04.pdf |publisher=owleducation.org |accessdate=12 November 2020}}</ref> It is an endangered plant species,<ref name=flora.on /> mainly threatened by the excessive [[nitrification]] of soils (due to the high density of seabirds) and invasive plant species, namely the [[Carpobrotus edulis|ice plant]].<ref name= owleducaction />

